<code>assert \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(size); (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i-1));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(size); (this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i-1)) || (\old(this.get(i)) == null && this.get(i) == null));</code>

This assertion ensures that for every valid index `i` starting from the insertion point `index` up to the old size of the list, the element at index `i` in the updated list is either equal to the element at index `i-1` in the old list, or both are `null`.
